        }
      ],
      "message": "silentpayments: return 0 instead of `ARG_CHECK`ing for empty inputs/outputs\n\nsecp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_prevouts_summary_create and\nsecp256k1_silentpayments_recipient_scan_outputs treated a transaction\nwithout eligible inputs or without taproot outputs as an illegal\nargument, which calls abort() by default. The API documentation says\nthey return 0 if the transaction is not a Silent Payments transaction,\nand callers scanning a block would have to special-case such\ntransactions.\n\nWith no public keys, the sum in prevouts_summary_create is the point at\ninfinity, so the existing check already returns 0. scan_outputs returns\n0 after argument validation and before the scan key is loaded.\n\nDiscovered by Anthropic's OSS Scanner, as vulnerability ANT-2026-25O0CNV8.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-31T09:35:21Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-31T08:04:57Z"
      },
