        }
      ],
      "message": "silentpayments: allow NULL arrays in scan_outputs if n_tx_outputs is 0\n\nSince the previous commit, scan_outputs accepts a transaction without\ntaproot outputs and returns 0. It still required tx_outputs and\nfound_outputs to be non-NULL, so a caller passing an empty array as\nNULL (e.g., data() of an empty std::vector in C++) would still abort.\n\nNeither array is dereferenced if n_tx_outputs is 0, so only check them\nfor NULL if n_tx_outputs > 0, and drop their SECP256K1_ARG_NONNULL\nattributes. This matches how prevouts_summary_create and\nsender_create_outputs treat empty key arrays.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Sebastian Falbesoner",
        "email": "sebastian.falbesoner@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-31T09:35:39Z"
      },
