      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "ACK 160590d1922914ddabe7c4d39fe14846b009212e\n\nI built the head and master (b88cbc7) with CMake and Apple clang 21, and `tests -t=silentpayments` and the example pass on both. A small program calls the two functions with an empty input or output set and a counting illegal callback. On master each call fires the callback, which by default aborts. On the head each returns 0 without it, the summary is zeroed and `*n_found_outputs` is 0. The tests are built with `SECP256K1_BUILD`, which turns `SECP256K1_ARG_NONNULL` off, so they cannot see the header change. I compiled a caller passing NULL arrays with `n_tx_outputs` 0 under `-Wnonnull -Werror`: it fails on master and builds on the head. The program, the commands and the output are in https://gist.github.com/fametrano/5f4db35678dfd8a5b4afd45803e92cca/4c6057f286d646f9ab235141d1155163794d65ae.\n\nThe new contract matches BIP352, where a transaction with no eligible input or no taproot output is not scanned, as with an input sum at infinity. The sender keeps its checks, in line with the BIP's MUST for at least one eligible input. To check the tests, I made six changes to `main_impl.h` one at a time. I put back each removed ARG_CHECK, made the two NULL checks unconditional, and removed the new early return and the `*n_found_outputs = 0`. Each change makes the module's tests fail, and the unchanged head passes.\n",
